  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Four letters are randomly posted in four letter boxes. Find the probability that at least one letterbox receives no letters.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{29}{32}$.\n\nSubtract the probability that every letterbox receives exactly one letter from 1.",
      "worked": "There are $4^4=256$ equally likely postings. If no letterbox is empty, each receives exactly one letter; there are $4\\times3\\times2\\times1=24$ such postings.\n\nLet $E$ be the event that at least one letterbox is empty.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(E)&=1-\\Pr(E')\\\\\\Pr(E)&=1-\\frac{24}{256}\\\\\\Pr(E)&=\\frac{232}{256}\\\\\\Pr(E)&=\\frac{29}{32}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
